Backlog tail, Selected item/items:

2. Contract verification and critical complaints support during bootstrap
'''
we define two asset buckets that have states, which we represent them with

clanker assets: [system cfg, shared cfg, all templates, all layouts]
clanker assets states: 
    clank-ok:
        all assets exits, config assets are convertible
    clank-bad
        any assets missing or non-convertible

pud assets: [config.yaml, all prog docs, the readme, and content dir]
pud assets states: 
    pud-ok: 
        all assets exits, config assets are convertible
    pud-empty: no pud assets exist
    pud-bad: : some but not all pud assets exist

we get matrix, which i flatten

co-po: execute bootstrap 
co-pe: offer clankerize 
co-pb: complain critically -> pud critical complaints, all soft complaints 
cb-po: complain critically, clanker crits, all soft complaints 
cb-pe: complain critically, clanker crits, all soft complaints 
cb-pb: complain critically, clanker crits, pud crits (from po perspective) all soft complaints 
'''
    [ ] 'content/core/presentation.py': declare ActionResult inheritors per info below
    [ ] 'content/core/engine_deps/ingestion.py':
        - expand Report abstract interface with get_critical_complaints
    [ ] 'content/modules/asset_ingestion/commons/error_collector.py':
        - update ErrorCollector to store critical complaints alongside non-critical complaints
             - both buckets have a getter and setter. (the Report interface has only getters)
    [ ] 'content/modules/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py':
        - implement helper to resolve clanker state
            - accept errorcollector, record any issue as critical complaint
            - return configs as dicts (default to {}), co | cb
        - implement helper to resolve pud state 
            -accept errorcollector, aggregate complains, and add to collector at end if pb case
            - returns config as dict, po | pe | pb
        - 'get_runtime_config'
            - remove NoConfig / ConfigAssembly exception raises from get_runtime_config and _get_validated_cfg_fragment
            - use helpers to get dicts, repo states
            - attempt execution of extractors, assemblers, and validators to amass non-critical complaints (helpers must return {} defaults for which critical complaints were recorded)
            - instantiate Actionresult spec given repo_states: 
                co-po: DoBootstrap
                co-po: OfferBootstrapWithComplaints (if ec has non-critical complaints)
                co-pe: OfferClankerize
                co-pe: OfferClankerizeWithComplaints (if ec has non-critical complaints)
                co-pb, cb-po, cb-pe, cb-pb: TerminateGracefully
            - return action_res, collector, button_map, ui_render, base_resolvers

    [ ] 'content/core/engine.py':
        - fold '_bootstrap' into 'run'
        - match on action_res type:
            DoBootstrap:
                - assign members to services, store ActionResult.BOOTSTRAP_SUCCESS on self, enter loop
            OfferBootstrapWithComplaints
                - pass report to self.helper, receive question to prompt user
                - store ActionResult.BOOTSTRAP_SUCCESS on self, enter loop
                - catch UserDecline, return ActionResult.MSG_DECLINED_BOOTSTRAP to halt program
            OfferClankerize
                - offer user to clankerize
                - call IngestionService.initialize_workspace
                - call IngestionService.get_runtime_config
                - assign members to services, store ActionResult.BOOTSTRAP_SUCCESS on self, enter loop
                - catch UserDecline, return ActionResult.MSG_DECLINED_INIT to halt program
            OfferClankerizeWithComplaints
                - pass report to self.helper, receive question to prompt user
                - offer user to clankerize
                - call IngestionService.initialize_workspace
                - call IngestionService.get_runtime_config
                - assign members to services, store ActionResult.BOOTSTRAP_SUCCESS on self, enter loop
                - catch UserDecline, return ActionResult.MSG_DECLINED_INIT to halt program
            TerminateGracefully
                - pass report to self.helper, receive ActionResult with complaints report formatted as msg
                - return actionresult to halt program

